<GuideLayout
  title="Silicone Transfer vs Screen Printing for Activewear Logos"
  type="BRANDING COMPARISON"
  description="Compare silicone transfer and screen printing for activewear logo customization by durability, stretch, texture, cost, MOQ and premium brand effect."
>
  <p>Logo application affects how professional a private label activewear product feels. Two common methods are silicone transfer and screen printing. Both can work, but they serve different brand positions and product types.</p>

  <h2>Silicone Transfer</h2>
  <p>Silicone transfer creates a raised, flexible and more premium-feeling logo. It works well for leggings, sports bras, hoodies and training sets where the brand wants a clean modern finish.</p>

  <h2>Screen Printing</h2>
  <p>Screen printing is often more cost-efficient for simple logos and larger quantity orders. It can be suitable for tops, bags, simple branding areas and promotional activewear programs.</p>

  <h2>How to Choose</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Choose silicone transfer for premium texture and stretch-friendly branding.</li>
    <li>Choose screen printing for simpler graphics and cost-sensitive programs.</li>
    <li>Always test logo placement after wash and stretch checks.</li>
  </ul>
</GuideLayout>
